From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: Implement TOM paragraph navigation.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

On offline Windows 10, both RichEdit classes and both windowless hosts
expand to the paragraphs containing the range, with an exclusive end
for a nonempty range. The implicit terminal mark counts, and unchanged
ranges return S_FALSE. Wine 11.22 returns E_NOTIMPL.

Use the editor's paragraph positions for the six tomParagraph methods.
Leave other units unchanged.

v2 (2026-11-26): Generate the patch context from the 11.22-3 series,
including textfont-applytmp. The implementation and test are unchanged.

v3 (2026-11-26): Offline Windows 10 results agree for both bitnesses and
all four hosts. Implement StartOf, EndOf, Move, MoveStart and MoveEnd in
addition to Expand. Collapse and movement count differ at the terminal
mark. Only MoveEnd and an extending EndOf can reach it via navigation.

v4 (2026-11-27): Promoted for Wine 11.23 with the verified strict
Wine test. The implementation is unchanged from the reviewed candidate.

